The second bound follows by the geometric recurrence; 3n epsilon_step<=1/2 is easily satisfied at N80. This applies to the word assembled from the computed local U,D blocks as well: inserting zero derivative blocks on other pulses gives the identical polynomial product. Let e=4096 epsilon_step. Both total U and each derivative D_j have operator error<=e. Since ||D_j||<=c and e<1, the approximate product -i U_approx* D_approx differs from (1)'s Hermitian matrix by at most e(c+e)+e<4e. Every normalized Pauli coefficient therefore has additional real uncertainty at most

